senses.gloss:
--a R. in the Sahya hill in दक्षिणापथ;
1: वा. ४५. १०४; Vi. II. 3. १२.
in भारतवर्ष; visited by बलराम from the Sahya hill;
2: भा. V. १९. १८; X. ७९. १२; Br. II. १६. ३४.
sacred to the पितृस्.
3: M. २२. ४५; ११४. २९.

(I)--(also भीम); a पाण्डव son of कुन्ती; father of श्रुतसेन; had another son घटोत्कच by हिदिम्बा, and a third Sarvagata by काली;
1: भा. IX. २२. २९-31; Vi. IV. १४. ३५; २०. ४०.
failed to hit the fish in लक्ष्मणा's स्वयम्वर;
2: Ib. X. ७१. २७; ५८. 4; ६४. 9.
joy at कृष्ण's visit to Indraprastha and कृष्ण's respects to him; was consoled by कृष्ण when banished to forest;
3: भा. X. ८३. २३.
sent to the western terri- tories with the Matsyas, Kekayas and Madrakas.
4: Ib. X. ७२. १३.
Advised by Uddhava to go in Brahmana's disguise to जरासन्ध and vanquish him; went with कृष्ण and Arjuna to Girivraja. After killing जरासन्ध, भीमसेन returned to हस्तिना- pura.
5: Ib. X. ७१. 7; ७२. ३२-46; ७३. ३१.
Declined to follow बलराम's advice not to fight; fought with Duryodhana at कुरुक्षेत्र and felled him with his गदा;
6: Ib. X. ७८ [९५(v)३९]; ७९. २३ and २८; I. 7. १३.
was in charge of cooking in the राजसूय of युधिष्ठिर;
7: Ib. X. ७५. 4.
fed धृतराष्ट्र; advocated killing of अश्वत्- थाम and felt sorry at कृष्ण's separation;
8: Ib. I. १३. २२; II. 7. ३५; I. 7. ५१ and ५४; 9. १५; १०. १०.
put an end to the राक्षसस् born of क्रोधवशा: propagator of भीमद्वा- दशीव्रत;
9: M. 6. ४३; ६९. १२-3.
gave पिण्ड sitting on his left leg to जनार्धन, [page२-565+ २४] and attained Brahmaloka with his brothers;
१०: वा. ८६. ४८; १०८. ९१.
strength of; depended on the good will of कृष्ण.
११: Vi. V. ३८. ३३.
